// ── Item-type classification (cleano_inventory_operations_fixes.pdf #1 + #4) ──
// ProductCategory answers "how did the cleaner USE this at clock-out?". It has
// no opinion on whether the thing is consumed at all, so a bucket and a bottle
// of Windex both landed on OTHER/LIQUID_SPRAY and ran through the same refill
// thresholds — which is why a cleaner holding exactly one scraper was told they
// were "running low". ItemType answers the different question "what KIND of
// thing is this?", and is what the reporting/threshold rules branch on.
enum ItemType {
  // Liquids & dilutables → reported as a level (Full/Good/Half/Low/Empty).
  LIQUID
  // Gloves, bags, rolls → reported as a quantity plus a status.
  COUNTABLE_CONSUMABLE
  // Scrapers, brooms, vacuums, mops, buckets → condition reporting only.
  // Refill thresholds never apply to these.
  REUSABLE_EQUIPMENT
}

// Reported level for a LIQUID item. Deliberately coarse — a cleaner eyeballs a
