enum JobBillingType {
  FLAT
  HOURLY
}

/// What KIND OF BUILDING a job is at (PDF #11, Stage 9). Distinct from the
/// service category in `Job.jobType`: a house clean and an apartment clean are
/// the same service, which is why the BookingKoala importer folds both onto
/// RESIDENTIAL — this column is where the property fact survives that fold.
/// Exactly the PDF's two options (decision D8); extending it later is an enum
/// add plus a label in `src/lib/property-type.ts`.
enum PropertyType {
  APARTMENT_CONDO
  HOUSE
}

/// Where a QUOTED booking is in its life before it becomes a normal job
/// (PDF #9, Stage 11). Post-construction is not priced instantly — the customer
/// pays a deposit, uploads photos, and an admin sets the real price afterwards.
///
///   PENDING_REVIEW  deposit paid, photos in, waiting for an admin to look
///   QUOTED          admin set a final price and emailed it to the customer
///   ACCEPTED        customer confirmed; from here it is an ordinary job
///   DECLINED        customer said no; the deposit disposition is a separate call
///
/// Deliberately NOT extra values on `JobStatus`: that enum drives clock-in,
/// payroll, invoicing, both calendars and a dozen admin filters, and a quote has
/// no business in any of them. A quote-pending job carries `status = CREATED`
/// AND `quoteStatus = PENDING_REVIEW`; the second column is what hides it from
/// cleaners. NULL = not a quote, which is every row that predates this stage.
/// See `src/lib/quote-status.ts`.
enum QuoteStatus {
  PENDING_REVIEW
  QUOTED
  ACCEPTED
  DECLINED
}

/// How a job's money is assembled — an ADMIN CHOICE, not a guess from
/// provenance (cleano_new_fixes.pdf fix 2). See `src/lib/job-money.ts`.
///
///   ITEMIZED     the parts ARE the price: `base + sum(add-on unit x qty)`,
///                then the discount, then tax. Adding an add-on raises what the
///                customer pays. Every admin-authored job starts here.
///   FINAL_PRICE  the admin (or the source system) typed ONE service total and
///                that total wins. Add-on rows are an ITEMISATION of it — they
///                are recorded for scope and for the cleaner, and they never
///                move the money. Every web booking and BookingKoala import is
///                stamped this way, because their stored subtotal already
///                contains the extras.
///
/// NULL means "never stamped" and falls back to `addOnMoneyBasis(bookingSource)`
/// — the implicit rule this enum replaces — so a row that predates the column
/// prices exactly as it did before.
enum JobPricingMode {
  ITEMIZED
  FINAL_PRICE
}

